 "response": "Studron's budget is now **$2590K**. Only the Finance Office's own budget changes count. Messages from Operations, Engineering, Vendor, Sales and other teams are ignored, as are Finance notes that don't change the budget.\n\n**Method**\n1. Start from the Finance Office base figure of $1870K (#0001).\n2. Resolve every chain of withdrawals from the latest record backwards. An update counts only if the withdrawal aimed at it has itself been cancelled. For example:\n   - #0066 cancels #0031, which revives #0013, which cancels #0008. So #0006 (\u2212$77K) still applies.\n   - #0522 cancels #0472, which revives #0107. Following that chain through means #0011 stays in force, so #0004 (+$27K) is removed.\n   - #1594 cancels #1542, so #1366 (\u2212$69K) still applies.\n   - #1570 withdraws #1053, so that +$527K does not count.\n3. Add every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in order.\n\n**Checkpoints in the running total**\n- After #0110: $3715K\n- After #0441: $4954K\n- After #0799: $2975K\n- After #1053 (withdrawn): $2304K\n- After #1600: $2590K\n\nThis is a long running total done by hand over about 1,600 records. A slip in one withdrawal chain or one addition would change the result.\n\nANSWER: $2590K",
